at a time when the markets are giving  many investors a rough ride warren  buffett is buying the dip  the billionaire investor is adding  several new major positions to his  portfolio as his investing conglomerate  berkshire hathaway deployed more than 51  billion dollars into stocks during the  first quarter of 2022 this is  berkshire's biggest quarterly spending  spree in recent history among the major  purchases were 55 million shares of  citigroup worth about 2.6 billion  dollars and 69 million shares of  paramount global worth around 1.9  billion dollars berkshire also made  sizable purchases in two energy  companies chevron and occidental  petroleum legacy tech company hp and  video game company activision blizzard  the total shares held by berkshire for  those companies are now roughly 159  million for chevron worth about 27  billion dollars 143 million for  occidental worth about 10 billion  121 million hp shares worth over 4  billion dollars and 64 million shares of  activision worth about 5 billion  berkshire also notably exited 2 large  stakes in the first quarter of 2022  buffett sold all of his shares in wells  fargo which had previously been a top  holding and part of his portfolio since  1989. he also sold nearly all of his 8  billion stake in telecom giant verizon  holding just 1.4 million shares at the  end of march way down from the more than  150 million shares he owned at the end  of december 2021 buffett remains a top  contender on the forbes list being the  fifth richest person in the world with a  net worth of about 113 billion dollars  [Music]
 

